# Commit Messages — TOKEN-NNN Index

Every git commit in this repo must start with a **TOKEN-NNN** prefix (3-digit, zero-padded). These are local change indexes for tracking — not Jira/Linear tickets.

## Format

```text
TOKEN-NNN: Imperative summary sentence.

Optional body when the why is not obvious.
```

## Rules

* Prefix is **required** on every commit the agent creates
* One logical change per commit; new index for each commit
* Before committing, run `git log --oneline -20` and use the next free number (max existing + 1). This batch starts at `TOKEN-001` if none exist yet
* Summary: imperative mood, ≤72 chars after the prefix
* Do not squash unrelated work under one TOKEN id

## Examples

```text
TOKEN-001: Add shared outbound REST infrastructure in tokenrealty-web.

TOKEN-002: Extend ServiceRestClientBuilder with timeout and trace propagation.

TOKEN-003: Migrate marketplace PaymentClient to DownstreamRestClientSupport.
```

## When committing for the user

1. Split staged work into logical commits
2. Assign sequential TOKEN-NNN ids
3. Push only when explicitly asked (user may ask commit + push together)

